                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This review contains spoilers.\r\n\r\nI would like to commend the game firstly on how pretty it is, there are so many hidden ponds and water sources that would just be downright delightful to hang out in.\r\nI have nothing else to commend the game for.\r\n\r\nThe premise shows promise, playing as a vulnerable young woman who has been kidnapped in a lush mediterranean environment is the thing that initially hooked me, why was she kidnapped? Who are the kidnappers and what are there goals?\r\nWell.. it's socialism. The goal of the big bad is to run a socialist island, and all the inhumane acts that he performs is in service of this because... all socialists are evil? I have no idea.\r\nThe story is abysmal, The dialogue is incredibly poorly written with crazy wanderers spouting nonsense about \"chicken nuggets\" and how \"satan makes the daisies cry\" to the main character just making terrible jokes upon discovering acts of human depravity.\r\nVoice acting is mid at best, and I'm pretty sure that one of the major characters is text to speech with how robotic it sounds and how it pronounces words incorrectly, further proof of this claim is indiegala using generative ai to develop there newest game, so I wouldn't put such laziness past them.\r\nSurvival mechanics boil down to crafting healing items and weapons, drinking water and killing creatures to expand inventory space.\r\nCombat isn't fun, I played on the harder difficulty and just used the crowbar to kill goats and foxes as fighting humanoids was often not nearly worth the trouble, you eventually get a crossbow that is capable of one shotting every enemy except bosses, bosses having so much health that they are just frustrating to fight.\r\nPlatforming is just hanging off rocks and ledges and aiming the crosshair at the white paint on the next ledge and waiting for the crosshair to change so you can safely magentize to it.\r\nMusic is all over the place, the dying light influence is clear from the innapropriate synthwave or the generic buttrock, the game would often play \"scary\" music when literally nothing was happening just to remind you that you're supposed to be experiencing a tense and atmospheric game. The music system is also broken and clearly has music tracks mapped to certain areas, however these areas have hard borders, so you can move back and forth over these borders to repeatedly stop and start music tracks.\r\n\r\nHonorable mentions:\r\n- one of the characters wears a shirt with the troll face on it.\r\n- the wise old caretaker of the island asks you to give him sexual favors upon meeting him.\r\n- the game features a metal gear style post credits scene of 2 characters talking about future espionage, but 1000 times dumber.\r\n\r\nAnd finally a word about the developers themselves.\r\nThey currently have 2 games in early access, 1 hasn't been updated in 3 years, the other in 2 years, Despite this they are pushing a playtest for a gen ai game.",
